<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>PAYE tax bands for resident individuals, from 1 July 2023 (Kenya Revenue Authority; Finance Act 2023):</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Monthly taxable pay (Ksh)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Rate</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">First <m>24\,000</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>10\%</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Next <m>8333</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>25\%</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Next <m>467\,667</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>30\%</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Next <m>300\,000</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>32.5\%</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Above <m>800\,000</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>35\%</m></cell></row></tabular><p>Personal relief: Ksh <m>2400</m> a month, taken off the tax. PAYE is never negative.</p><p>For each monthly taxable pay, choose the highest rate at which any part of it is taxed.</p><p>(a) Ksh <m>{812\,000}</m> [ 10% | 25% | 30% | 32.5% | 35% ]  </p><p>(b) Ksh <m>{18\,500}</m> [ 10% | 25% | 30% | 32.5% | 35% ]  </p><p>(c) Ksh <m>{32\,333}</m> [ 10% | 25% | 30% | 32.5% | 35% ]  </p><p>(d) Ksh <m>{74\,000}</m> [ 10% | 25% | 30% | 32.5% | 35% ]  </p><p>(e) Ksh <m>{520\,000}</m> [ 10% | 25% | 30% | 32.5% | 35% ]  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The band edges are <m>24\,000</m>, <m>32\,333</m>, <m>500\,000</m> and <m>800\,000</m>. A pay exactly at the top of a band stays in that band.</p><ul><li>(a) Ksh <m>{812\,000}</m>: Pay above <m>800\,000</m> is taxed at <m>35\%</m>.</li><li>(b) Ksh <m>{18\,500}</m>: All of it is in the first band, up to <m>24\,000</m>.</li><li>(c) Ksh <m>{32\,333}</m>: The <m>25\%</m> band runs up to <m>24\,000 + 8333 = 32\,333</m> exactly.</li><li>(d) Ksh <m>{74\,000}</m>: It is between <m>32\,333</m> and <m>500\,000</m>: the top slice is taxed at <m>30\%</m>.</li><li>(e) Ksh <m>{520\,000}</m>: <m>20\,000</m> shillings are above <m>500\,000</m>, in the <m>32.5\%</m> band.</li></ul></p></solution>
    <answer><p>35%</p></answer>
    <answer><p>10%</p></answer>
    <answer><p>25%</p></answer>
    <answer><p>30%</p></answer>
    <answer><p>32.5%</p></answer>
</stack-static>